=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/DevTools (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/DevTools   kind=page   web route=/dev-tools
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/DevToolsPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/DevToolsPage/ (+ NavigationView registration, test, ledger)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- Layout mapping: this repo's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files). Every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection, unit-tested
  headlessly via linked Compile items in TeslaSync.App.Tests), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder)
  and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view) — exactly as the sibling W7 ApiPlaygroundPage / ApiLogsPage do. The generated prompt's
  idealized "TeslaSync/Features/Admin/DevToolsPage.xaml + DevToolsPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto these real conventions.
  Namespace = TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Admin (aligns with RouteGroup.AdminDevTools).
- Scope: the manifest scopes this unit to requiredCount=2 (strings devtools.title / devtools.subtitle) with NO data
  sources / NO panels — because web DevToolsPage.tsx is itself a thin compositional shell: a PageContainer header over a
  TabNav that swaps between five SECTION components (FleetApiSection, FleetTelemetryHealth, InfrastructureSection,
  ClientUtilitiesSection, ReferenceLinksSection). The page's OWN regions = the header + the 5-tab navigator + the
  per-tab content host; the section internals are their own (separately-built) units. This port reproduces that shell.
- Header (web PageContainer title/subtitle): the shared native PageContainer surface carries the localized title and
  subtitle — the two parity strings (devtools.title="Developer Tools", devtools.subtitle="Fleet API, telemetry,
  infrastructure & utilities"), both already present in Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw and asserted by the test.
- Tab navigator (web TabNav): a Fluent TabView (TsTabs) with five TabViewItems in the exact web TABS order — Fleet API,
  Telemetry, Infrastructure, Utilities, Reference — each header carrying a Segoe Fluent glyph mirroring the web lucide
  icon (Globe / Radio / Server / Wrench / BookOpen) + a localized label (devtools.tab.* keys; the web hardcodes the
  labels, the native port routes them through the localizer so no literal ships in the view, ADR-014). Tab labels and
  order are projected by DevToolsCatalog and bound through DevToolsPageViewModel; sections mount lazily on selection.
- Section composition (the per-tab content host = web the FadeIn that renders the active section):
  · Fleet API     → DevToolsFleetApiSection — a native port of FleetApiSection.tsx: the seven-step Setup Wizard
    (DevToolsOnboardingWizard over ONBOARDING_STEPS) + the Fleet API Tools grid (Config, Partner Registration, Partner
    Public Key, Public Key Setup, Vehicle Key Pairing, Telemetry Subscribe, Telemetry Config, Fleet Status, Vehicle
    Data) — each a shared ToolCard wrapping its inputs / action buttons / ResultPanel. Tools fire through an injected
    DevToolsToolRunner; the default offline runner surfaces an honest "backend not reachable" result (ADR-011, never a
    blank panel), the WinUI analogue of the web sections mounting against an un-provisioned origin.
  · Telemetry     → FleetTelemetryHealth.Create(...)             (delivered section; data-backed)
  · Infrastructure→ FeatureViews.Infrastructure.InfrastructureSection.Create(...) (delivered devtools section)
  · Utilities     → ClientUtilities.ClientUtilitiesSection.Create(localizer)      (delivered; static tool catalog)
  · Reference     → ReferenceLinksSection(localizer)                              (delivered; static link catalog)
  The two data-backed sections bind through the shared data layer (a GeneratedApiClient over a 5s-timeout HttpClient +
  a process-local DevToolsMemoryCacheStore implementing ICacheStore); with no reachable origin they render their OWN
  honest loading / empty / error states (ADR-013) — the same empty-feed behaviour the whole W7 layer ships today.
- No hardcoded colours/typography — DisplayTokens / TypographyTokens drive light/dark/high-contrast from W1; every
  visible string flows through ILocalizer.GetString(key, fallback); panels carry AutomationProperties names; the
  TabView + ToolCards inherit keyboard + Narrator semantics; no custom animation (reduced-motion honoured implicitly).
- Build prerequisite (W1, ADR-004): the generated C# client (apps/windows/Generated/, gitignored) was regenerated via
  apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts and compiled by a local Generated.csproj so TeslaSync.App.Core / .App resolve the
  TeslaSync.Windows.Generated.Api namespace. Both are gitignored local artifacts, not part of this changeset.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=2
- [x] string — devtools.title
      key  : DevToolsCatalog.TitleKey = "devtools.title"  (feature-views/DevToolsPage/DevToolsPage.Model.cs)
      bind : DevToolsCatalog.Title(localizer) → localizer.GetString("devtools.title", "Developer Tools");
             surfaced by DevToolsPageViewModel.Title and rendered into the PageContainer header by DevToolsPage.cs.
      resw : translation.devtools.title = "Developer Tools"  (apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw:8487)
      test : DevToolsPageTests.Catalog_resolves_every_manifest_string_key (records the key),
             DevToolsPageTests.Manifest_keys_match_the_web_source,
             DevToolsPageTests.Manifest_strings_resolve_the_web_defaults (asserts "Developer Tools").
- [x] string — devtools.subtitle
      key  : DevToolsCatalog.SubtitleKey = "devtools.subtitle"  (feature-views/DevToolsPage/DevToolsPage.Model.cs)
      bind : DevToolsCatalog.Subtitle(localizer) → localizer.GetString("devtools.subtitle",
             "Fleet API, telemetry, infrastructure & utilities"); surfaced by DevToolsPageViewModel.Subtitle and
             rendered as the PageContainer subtitle by DevToolsPage.cs.
      resw : translation.devtools.subtitle = "Fleet API, telemetry, infrastructure & utilities"
             (apps/windows/Strings/en/Resources.resw:8484)
      test : DevToolsPageTests.Catalog_resolves_every_manifest_string_key (records the key),
             DevToolsPageTests.Manifest_keys_match_the_web_source,
             DevToolsPageTests.Manifest_strings_resolve_the_web_defaults (asserts the web default).
PARITY_COVERED=2

